  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b000001",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 1,
      "end_line": 1,
      "raw": "# iiLocalLLM\n",
      "level": 1,
      "title": "iiLocalLLM"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000002",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 2,
      "end_line": 2,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 3,
      "end_line": 6,
      "raw": "The service exposes a model-neutral text embedding interface for explicitly\ndeclared embedding models, including a native GGUF runtime implementation.\nSee [text embeddings](docs/Embeddings.md) for model capability, pooling,\nresource and verification boundaries.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000004",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 7,
      "end_line": 7,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 8,
      "end_line": 10,
      "raw": "C++23 local model management and inference. Version **0.56.0** separates the\nagent/MCP harness into [iiMultimodalAgent](../iiMultimodalAgent/README.md).\niiLocalLLM no longer discovers, links or exports iiDecision or agent code.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000006",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 11,
      "end_line": 11,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000007",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 12,
      "end_line": 17,
      "raw": "It retains model manifests/catalogs, pulling/verification, hardware and residency\npolicy, service scheduling, context caching, native llama.cpp/libmtmd\ntext/image/audio/timestamped-frame inference, optional MLX, parameters, IPC, HTTP\nand generic RpcHandler extension interfaces. Existing Qt 6.8.3 Core/Network public\ncontracts remain. Native llama.cpp runs in-process; the separately selected\nexisting MLX worker retains its Python requirement.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000008",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 18,
      "end_line": 18,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000009",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 19,
      "end_line": 19,
      "raw": "## Build and consume\n",
      "level": 2,
      "title": "Build and consume"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000010",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 20,
      "end_line": 20,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000011",
      "kind": "fenced_code",
      "start_line": 21,
      "end_line": 28,
      "raw": "```sh\ncmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \\\n  -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=\"<iiFileProvider and Qt prefixes>\" \\\n  -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=\"$HOME/.local/SDK/iiLocalLLM\"\ncmake --build build --parallel 4\nctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure\ncmake --install build\n```\n",
      "language": "sh",
      "code": "cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \\\n  -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=\"<iiFileProvider and Qt prefixes>\" \\\n  -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=\"$HOME/.local/SDK/iiLocalLLM\"\ncmake --build build --parallel 4\nctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure\ncmake --install build\n",
      "closed": true
    },
    {
      "id": "b000012",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 29,
      "end_line": 29,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000013",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 30,
      "end_line": 32,
      "raw": "`./install.sh` also verifies an independent installed consumer. Backend settings\nand inference fixtures retain their IILOCALLLM_* options. No iiDecision accelerator\npackages are required by an inference-only consumer.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000014",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 33,
      "end_line": 33,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000015",
      "kind": "fenced_code",
      "start_line": 34,
      "end_line": 37,
      "raw": "```cmake\nfind_package(iiLocalLLM 0.56 CONFIG REQUIRED)\ntarget_link_libraries(MyApp PRIVATE iiLocalLLM::iiLocalLLM)\n```\n",
      "language": "cmake",
      "code": "find_package(iiLocalLLM 0.56 CONFIG REQUIRED)\ntarget_link_libraries(MyApp PRIVATE iiLocalLLM::iiLocalLLM)\n",
      "closed": true
    },
    {
      "id": "b000016",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 38,
      "end_line": 38,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000017",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 39,
      "end_line": 41,
      "raw": "Use `<iiLocalLLM.h>` and `iiLocalLLM::Service`. Inference-only iiLocalLLMD,\niilocal-llm-service and iillm remain here. Agent startup and CLI commands move to\niiMultimodalAgentD, iimagent-service, iimagent, iimagent-mcp and iimagent-plugins.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000018",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 42,
      "end_line": 42,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000019",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 43,
      "end_line": 46,
      "raw": "Agent users must rebuild against iiMultimodalAgent::iiMultimodalAgent, include\n`<iiMultimodalAgent.h>` or `<iiMultimodalAgent/agent/Engine.h>`, and use\n`iiMultimodalAgent::agent` / `iiMultimodalAgent::mcp`. Persisted schemas and wire\nmethods stay stable. The minor version advances because the combined ABI changes.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000020",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 47,
      "end_line": 47,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000021",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 48,
      "end_line": 52,
      "raw": "See [module migration](docs/ModuleExtraction.md), [architecture](docs/Architecture.md),\n[model management](docs/ModelManagement.md), [hardware](docs/HardwarePolicy.md),\n[parameters](docs/Parameters.md), [HTTP](docs/HTTP.md), [IPC](docs/IPC.md), and\n[Windows](docs/WindowsBuildAndRun.md). Old harness documentation links now point\nto their owning package; historical test counts are not new verification claims.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000022",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 53,
      "end_line": 53,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000023",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 54,
      "end_line": 56,
      "raw": "Pruned Nemotron Bolt GGUFs use a guarded upstream backport for per-layer expert\ndimensions. [Nemotron Bolt](docs/NemotronBolt.md) documents the native CPU\nregression fixture and the separate service residency-budget boundary.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000024",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 57,
      "end_line": 57,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000025",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 58,
      "end_line": 62,
      "raw": "Hosts can use `createLlamaRuntime(LlamaRuntimeOptions)` to copy weights into owned\nmemory and cap GPU layer offload without exposing device selection to model\nmanifests or clients. The native Metal regression covers batched top-9 expert\nrouting. See [Nemotron Bolt](docs/NemotronBolt.md) for the verified agent greeting,\nmemory limits, and residency settings.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000026",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 63,
      "end_line": 63,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000027",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 64,
      "end_line": 64,
      "raw": "## License\n",
      "level": 2,
      "title": "License"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000028",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 65,
      "end_line": 65,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000029",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 66,
      "end_line": 66,
      "raw": "SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000030",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 67,
      "end_line": 67,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000031",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 68,
      "end_line": 70,
      "raw": "The original code and documentation in this repository are licensed under the\n[MIT License](LICENSE). Third-party code, libraries, fonts, tools, and model\nweights retain their respective licenses.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000032",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 71,
      "end_line": 71,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000033",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 72,
      "end_line": 72,
      "raw": "Related implementation contracts: [Native tool-turn contracts](docs/NativeToolTemplates.md).\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000034",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 73,
      "end_line": 73,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000035",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 74,
      "end_line": 74,
      "raw": "Managed MLX environments build a validated Transformers import index to avoid repeated model-source scans during worker startup. See [MLX import metadata](docs/MlxImportIndex.md) for preparation, invalidation and unchanged inference deadlines.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000036",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 75,
      "end_line": 75,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000037",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 76,
      "end_line": 76,
      "raw": "Model integrity still verifies every byte; the macOS streaming SHA-256 path uses the system implementation. See [model integrity](docs/ModelIntegrity.md).\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000038",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 77,
      "end_line": 77,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000039",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 78,
      "end_line": 78,
      "raw": "Source and adjacent headers are grouped by responsibility under `src/`; installed flat include names remain unchanged. See [source layout](docs/SourceLayout.md).\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000040",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 79,
      "end_line": 79,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
